--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-reject-malformed-json-pointer-tokens.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-reject-malformed-json-pointer-tokens
+type: decision-log
+title: "Reject malformed JSON Pointer tokens"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6901 permits only `~0` and `~1` escape sequences in reference tokens. Accepting other uses of
+`~` would silently resolve a different, non-standard pointer.
+
+## Decision
+
+Reject a pointer when any token contains a tilde escape other than `~0` or `~1`. A pointer must also
+be the empty string or begin with `/`; array indices must use the RFC's canonical decimal syntax.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers receive an error for malformed pointers rather than ambiguous results. The resolver remains
+strictly interoperable with RFC 6901 producers.
